//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_SYMINFO_MINCONTRACT", overlay = false)

// W9-T4-F1 -- THE CAPTURE THAT SETTLES `syminfo.mincontract`, per exchange.
//
// Pine v6 reference, `syminfo.mincontract` (simple float): "The smallest amount
// of the current symbol that can be traded. This limit is set by the exchange.
// For cryptocurrencies, it is often less than 1 token. For most other types of
// asset, it is often 1."  "Often" is not "always", so the engine serves no value
// until this probe is captured on a witness of each exchange in our store's
// spelling (`symbolScope.json::min_contract`): NYSE:RDDT (the Q-S1a capture
// symbol), NASDAQ:AAPL and AMEX:SPY (NYSE Arca), the witnesses `tick_size` and
// `listing_fields` already hold.
//
// A VALUE capture (`docs/pine/capture-procedure.md`): read the plot values, never
// the CSV. Each capture becomes one `min_contract` row with all five of
// {value, witnesses, captured, how, captures}; `symbolScopeMinContract.test.js`
// re-reads it and requires M01 == value on EVERY bar.

plot(syminfo.mincontract, "M01_mincontract")
// M02 -- the reciprocal, so a sub-unit answer (a crypto pair: 1e-8 and the like)
// is readable at full precision even if a plot rounds the raw value.
plot(1 / syminfo.mincontract, "M02_inverse")
// NON-VACUITY CONTROL: a dead study and an answer of 0 cannot wear the same row.
plot(str.length(syminfo.ticker), "M03_len_ticker_CONTROL")
